    "\n",
    "# English\n",
    "## Deterministic Controller (Deterministic_controller folder)\n",
    "### Introduction\n",
    "The idea is to use a deterministic controller.\n",
    "\n",
    "The core of this method is that a grayscale mask is applied to the image and four horizontal zones (<a id=\"ROI\"></a>**ROI**: Region Of Interest)) are created.\n",
    "\n",
    "Within the simulation, if the displays are enabled, you can see separately:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Before (Without Mask) | After (With Mask) |\n",
    "| :---: | :---: |\n",
    "| ![display_without_mask](raw_display.png) | ![display_with_mask](mask_display.png) |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Masked Display\n",
    "#### Elements Inside\n",
    "\n",
    "The rectangles:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Blue.\n",
    "- Yellow.\n",
    "- Green.\n",
    "- Orange.\n",
    "\n",
    "These are the Regions of Interest discussed above.\n",
    "\n",
    "The targets of the same colors are the centroids of the black color within the regions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The red and purple vertical lines represent the center line and the error line, respectively, and are calculated as:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Red line:\n",
    "\n",
    "    $$\n",
    "    x_{RL} = \\frac{w_C}{2}\n",
    "    $$\n",
    "\n",
    "    where:\n",
    "\n",
    "    - $x_{RL}$: x position of the red line;\n",
    "    - $w_C$: Width of the Camera in pixels\n",
    "\n",
    "- Purple line:\n",
    "\n",
    "    $$\n",
    "    x_{PL} = x_{RL} + \\epsilon\n",
    "    $$\n",
    "\n",
    "    where:\n",
    "\n",
    "    - $x_{PL}$: x position of the purple line;\n",
    "    - $\\epsilon$: is the weighted error derived from the centroids calculated as:\n",
    "    \n",
    "        $$\n",
    "        \\epsilon = \\sum_{i=1}^4 {\\epsilon_i*weight_i}\n",
    "        $$\n",
    "\n",
    "        where:\n",
    "        - $\\epsilon_i$: is the error of the centroid of the single region;\n",
    "        - $weight_i$: is the weight used for the single region. By default, the values are set as\n",
    "\n",
    "        |Blue Zone (Top)|Yellow Zone (Upper Center)|Green Zone (Lower Center)|Orange Zone (Bottom)|\n",
    "        | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n",
    "        |0.15|0.25|0.25|0.35|\n",
    "\n",
    "You can find the calculations in the functions:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `find_centroid()`;\n",
    "- `compute_final_error()`.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### How is the mask created?\n",
    "\n",
    "**(Dunno, I'll check now)**\n",
    "\n",
    "Acquires the image ➔ Converts to a BGRA array ➔ Converts to grayscale (by averaging the RGB values)\n",
    "\n",
    "You can find it in the function:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `get_gray_image()`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Steering Calculation\n",
    "\n",
    "The steering calculation is handled by a PID (Proportional-Integral-Derivative) controller. For those who don't know:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{align}\n",
    "P &= K_p*\\epsilon \\\\\n",
    "I &= K_i \\int \\epsilon \\,dt \\\\\n",
    "D &= K_d\n",
    " \\frac{d\\epsilon}{dt}\n",
    "\\end{align}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "In this case, the simple_pid library was used and the parameters have the values:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $K_p = 0.05$\n",
    "- $K_i = 0.0$\n",
    "- $K_d = 0.0$\n",
    "\n",
    "So in practice, a **Proportional** controller is used, determined by a heuristic method (actually, I just fiddled with it until it worked, but I wanted to sound cool).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Saved Data\n",
    "Simulation data is saved in the Log folder in CSV and JSON formats. These are used to perform data analysis and understand how one controller behaves compared to another. Saving can be disabled using boolean variables inside the controllers.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **CSV**: contains data in a dataframe where columns represent variables and rows represent the values of those variables."
   ]
